{
  "title": "Everyday verbs: ます forms",
  "note": "Polite verbs end in ます. The ます form covers both present and future: 行きます \"I go\" or \"I will go.\" Negative: ません. Invitation: ませんか \"Won't you...?\" Suggestion: ましょう \"Let's...\" The verb goes at the end of the sentence. 分かります takes が: 日本語が分かります.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide: Polite Form and Verb Stems",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar/polite"
  },
  "items": [
